.Dd October 31, 2026
.Dt REFINEID 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm refineid
.Nd Finnish identity card tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Ar command
.Op Ar argument ...
.Nm
.Ar command
.Cm help
.Nm
.Fl V | Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads, manages and signs with a FINEID card, the Finnish identity card,
in a PC/SC reader or in a phone paired with
.Nm
.Cm phone pair .
.Pp
Without a command, or with
.Cm help ,
.Fl h
or
.Fl -help ,
.Nm
lists the everyday commands, one line each;
.Nm
.Cm expert
lists the advanced ones.
.Nm
.Ar command
.Cm help ,
or
.Fl h
or
.Fl -help
among a command's arguments, shows that command's options.
.Nm
.Cm card help ,
.Nm
.Cm pin help ,
.Nm
.Cm document help ,
.Nm
.Cm phone help ,
.Nm
.Cm cert help
and
.Nm
.Cm reader help
list a group's commands.
.Pp
A command word may be shortened to any prefix that names one command:
.Nm
.Cm doc s
is
.Nm
.Cm document sign .
A prefix that fits several commands is refused with the candidates.
Scripts spell commands out; a prefix that is unique today may not be
after a command is added.
.Pp
The commands fall into groups:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm card
The card: readout, eMRTD data, raw signatures, decryption and public
keys.
.It Cm pin
The card's PINs: activation, change and unblock.
.It Cm document
Signed documents a counterparty can open.
.It Cm phone
The paired phone, whose card the computer uses over the network.
.It Cm verify , cert
Offline signature and certificate tools.
.It Cm reader
The card reader itself.
.El
.Pp
A command acting on a card targets one card; when several cards are
connected,
.Fl -reader Ar substr
narrows the choice to readers whose name contains
.Ar substr .
PINs are always read from the terminal, never from the command line,
and nothing is echoed while one is typed.
.Pp
An operation, a command that changes the card, a file or the pairing,
prints nothing when it succeeds: the PIN prompt is all it shows.
With
.Fl v
it prints its step report on the standard output.
A query, such as
.Cm card ,
.Cm phone ,
.Cm verify
or
.Cm cert show ,
prints its result.
Errors go to the standard error, and the exit status tells success from
failure; see
.Sx EXIT STATUS .
.Sh OPTIONS
These options are global.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
As the first argument, list the commands; after a command, show its
options.
.It Fl V , Fl -version
Print the version and exit.
No command prints the version otherwise.
.It Fl v , Fl -verbose
Show what each step did.
Without it an operation prints nothing on success.
Recognised anywhere on the command line, so no option value can be
spelled like it.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm card
.Op Fl -offline
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Op Fl -can Ar can | Fl -no-can
.Op Fl -crl-file Ar path
.Op Fl -save-cert Ar dir
.Op Fl -remote
.Xc
Per-card readout: certificates, chain walk and revocation, PIN retry
counters, and with
.Fl -can
the eMRTD section.
With no card in a reader, reads the card through the paired phone.
Without
.Fl -can
or
.Fl -no-can
on a terminal, prompts for the CAN; an empty answer skips the eMRTD
section.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -offline
Skip every network fetch.
.It Fl -can Ar can
The card access number printed on the card front; enables eMRTD.
.It Fl -no-can
Skip the eMRTD section without a prompt.
.It Fl -crl-file Ar path
Use a pre-fetched CRL instead of fetching one over HTTP.
.It Fl -save-cert Ar dir
Write each slot's certificate DER to
.Ar dir .
.It Fl -remote
Read the card through the paired phone only.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm pin activate
.Op Cm 1 | 2
.Op Fl -allow-reactivate
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Xc
First-time DVV card activation.
Prompts for the activation PIN, then the new PIN 1 and PIN 2, PIN 1
set first; with
.Cm 1
or
.Cm 2 ,
only that PIN.
The card is fully active once both are set; after one PIN, a line on
the standard error says when the other still looks unactivated.
Wrong tries consume the activation PIN's retry counter; locking it
leaves recovery to the separately orderable paid PUK.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -allow-reactivate
Run on a card whose PIN already looks activated.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm pin change
.Cm 1 | 2
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Op Fl -can Ar can
.Xc
Rotate PIN 1, the authentication PIN, or PIN 2, the qualified-signature
PIN.
Prompts for the current PIN, then the new PIN twice.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -can Ar can
The card access number; needed on the contactless interface.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm pin unblock
.Cm 1 | 2
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Xc
Unblock PIN 1 or PIN 2 with the PUK and set a new PIN.
A wrong PUK decrements the PUK counter; exhausting it permanently
bricks the card.
.It Xo
.Cm document sign
.Ar file ...
.Op Fl -format Ar format
.Op Fl -out Ar path
.Op Fl -slot Cm qualified | auth
.Op Fl -reason Ar text
.Op Fl -location Ar text
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Op Fl -can Ar can
.Op Fl -no-stamp
.Op Fl -timestamp Ar url ...
.Xc
Sign
.Ar file
into a format a counterparty can open.
Several files go into one container under one signature.
PIN2 and the qualified-signature key are used by default.
Signs at the highest level the format supports: LTA, embedded
evidence plus an archive timestamp, for
.Cm pades
and
.Cm asice-cades ;
LT, embedded evidence, for the rest.
There is no lower level.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -format Ar format
.Bl -tag -width "cades-detached" -compact
.It Cm pades
signature inside the PDF
.It Cm cades
CMS, document attached
.It Cm cades-detached
CMS, document left outside
.It Cm asice | bdoc
ASiC-E container with XAdES; one format, two names
.It Cm asice-cades
ASiC-E container with CAdES
.El
The default is
.Cm pades
for one PDF and
.Cm asice
otherwise.
The one-file formats refuse a set of files.
.It Fl -out Ar path
The finished document.
The default is beside the first
.Ar file ,
named
.Dq Ar stem Ns -signed- Ns Ar time . Ns Ar ext
with the UTC time, and stem
.Dq portfolio
for several files.
.It Fl -slot Cm qualified | auth
The key to sign with; qualified by default.
.It Fl -reason Ar text
The PAdES /Reason.
.It Fl -location Ar text
The PAdES /Location.
.It Fl -can Ar can
The card access number; required on the contactless interface.
.It Fl -timestamp Ar url
An RFC 3161 timestamp authority URL, or a named set.
The default is
.Lk http://timestamp.sectigo.com/qualified .
Repeat for alternatives; a failed answer is skipped, and signing fails
when none remains.
.Fl -timestamp Cm eu-qualified
names public EU endpoints.
.It Fl -no-stamp
No visible mark on the page; the signature stays invisible.
By default a PAdES signature puts a red seal on the last page asking the
reader to check the document's electronic signature.
Its middle lines are in the language of the locale, see
.Sx ENVIRONMENT ,
and its band carries the other two.
The seal names no one; the signature in the file is the evidence.
.El
.It Cm phone
Show the paired phone.
.It Cm phone pair
Pair with a phone running RefineID.
Start pairing on the phone and type the six-character code it shows.
The code is read from the prompt only, never from the command line.
.It Cm phone unpair
Forget the paired phone.
.El
.Sh ADVANCED COMMANDS
.Nm
.Cm expert
lists these: the card's raw keys and data, the test login through the
phone, offline certificate tools and the reader itself.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Cm card emrtd
.Fl -can Ar can
.Op Fl -save-face Ar path
.Op Fl -save-signature Ar path
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Xc
eMRTD file extraction: the same read as
.Cm card Fl -can ,
plus options that write artefacts to disk.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -can Ar can
The card access number printed on the card front.
.It Fl -save-face Ar path
Write the face image.
.It Fl -save-signature Ar path
Write the displayed-signature image.
.It Fl -reader Ar substr
Narrow to readers whose name contains
.Ar substr .
.El
.It Xo
.Cm card sign-auth | sign-qualified
.Fl -in Ar path
.Fl -out Ar path
.Op Fl -save-cert Ar path
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Op Fl -can Ar can
.Xc
Raw signature over a file:
.Cm sign-auth
with PIN1 and the authentication key,
.Cm sign-qualified
with PIN2 and the qualified-signature key.
The signature is verified locally against the on-card certificate.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -in Ar path
The input file.
.It Fl -out Ar path
The output file for the raw signature.
.It Fl -save-cert Ar path
Also write the signing certificate's DER.
.It Fl -can Ar can
The card access number; required on the contactless interface and
prompted for on a terminal when needed.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm card decrypt-auth
.Fl -in Ar path
.Fl -out Ar path
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Xc
Decrypt
.Fl -in
with PIN1 and the authentication key into
.Fl -out .
.It Xo
.Cm card pubkey
.Op Fl -slot Cm auth | qualified
.Op Fl -format Cm ssh | pem
.Op Fl -out Ar path
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Op Fl -comment Ar string
.Xc
Export the public key from an on-card certificate.
No PIN is needed.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -slot Cm auth | qualified
The key to export.
.It Fl -format Cm ssh | pem
An OpenSSH public key line or a PEM SubjectPublicKeyInfo.
.It Fl -out Ar path
Write all blocks to
.Ar path
instead of the standard output.
.It Fl -comment Ar string
The SSH comment; the default is the certificate's common name and
serial number.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm card export-all
.Ar dir
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Xc
Write every public artefact to
.Ar dir .
No PIN, no network.
.It Cm phone auth Op Ar url
Log in to a TLS site with the card in the paired phone and print the
response's status line.
.Ar url
defaults to
.Lk https://card.refineid.fi .
.It Xo
.Cm verify
.Fl -cert Ar path
.Fl -in Ar path
.Fl -sig Ar path
.Xc
Offline signature verification; reports ok or FAILED.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -cert Ar path
The certificate, PEM or DER, detected automatically.
.It Fl -in Ar path
The message that was signed.
.It Fl -sig Ar path
The raw signature.
.El
.It Cm cert show Ar path
Print a certificate's fields and its SHA-256 fingerprint.
PEM or DER, detected automatically.
.It Xo
.Cm cert chain
.Ar cert
.Op Fl -issuer-dir Ar dir
.Op Fl -aia-fetch
.Xc
Walk the certificate chain upward, verifying each child against its
issuer.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -issuer-dir Ar dir
A directory of candidate issuer certificates.
.It Fl -aia-fetch
Fetch missing issuers over HTTP via AIA caIssuers.
.El
.It Xo
.Cm reader keyboard
.Op Cm status | on | off
.Op Fl -reader Ar substr
.Xc
Show or set the keyboard (HID) interface of an ACS reader.
A phone hides its on-screen keyboard while the reader acts as a
keyboard.
The new mode takes effect when the reader is plugged in again.
Setting the mode prints nothing on success.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm status
Show the mode; the default.
.It Cm on
Keyboard and card reader.
.It Cm off
Card reader only.
.El
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev LC_ALL , LC_MESSAGES , LANG
The first one set and non-empty chooses the language of the seal
.Cm document sign
draws: Finnish for
.Li fi ,
Swedish for
.Li sv ,
English otherwise.
.It Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME , HOME , SNAP_USER_COMMON
Locate the pairing store; see
.Sx FILES .
.It Ev REFINEID_CA_BUNDLE
A CA bundle file for TLS connections, used instead of the system
bundle.
.It Ev SSL_CERT_FILE , SSL_CERT_DIR
Searched before the system bundle paths for the CA bundle of
.Cm phone auth .
.It Ev REFINEID_TLS_MAX
Set to
.Li 1.2
to cap TLS at version 1.2.
.It Ev REFINEID_PIN1 , REFINEID_PIN2
Read instead of the PIN prompt by
.Cm card sign-auth ,
.Cm card sign-qualified
and
.Cm document sign ,
only in a build with the
.Li pin-env-debug
feature.
.It Ev REFINEID_CURRENT_PIN1 , REFINEID_CURRENT_PIN2 , \
REFINEID_NEW_PIN1 , REFINEID_NEW_PIN2 , REFINEID_ACTIVATION_PIN
Read instead of the prompts by
.Cm pin change ,
.Cm pin unblock
and
.Cm pin activate ,
only in a build with the
.Li pin-env-debug
feature.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/refineid/rapp-pairs/
The pairing store: one owner-only file per paired phone, holding the
pairing's private key.
Without
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.Pa $HOME/.config/refineid/rapp-pairs/ ;
under a Snap,
.Pa $SNAP_USER_COMMON/.config/refineid/rapp-pairs/ .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 0
Success, or help or version shown on request.
.It 1
.Cm verify
rejected the signature, or
.Cm cert chain
reached no self-signed root, or
.Cm phone auth
received a 4xx or 5xx status; a redirect counts as success.
.It 64
The command line was not understood
.Pq Dv EX_USAGE .
.It 65
No PC/SC reader is connected.
.It 66
Readers are connected but no card is present.
.It 70
A transport, parse, signing or paired-phone failure
.Pq Dv EX_SOFTWARE .
.It 77
The card or local policy rejected a PIN or the PUK.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Read the card in the only reader:
.Dl $ refineid card
.Pp
Sign a PDF with the qualified-signature key:
.Dl $ refineid document sign report.pdf
.Pp
Show the options of one command:
.Dl $ refineid pin change help
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pcscd 8
.Rs
.%Q Digital and Population Data Services Agency
.%T FINEID specification
.%U https://dvv.fi/en/fineid-specifications
.Re
